 "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "The missed detection, as evidenced by the confidence score logs (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A), warrants a CAPA investigation to determine if design or software lifecycle processes need adjustment.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a non-recurrent ventricular tachycardia-adjacent irregularity detected by remote monitoring, with no adverse patient outcome recorded. While the clinician note documenting this event was not filed, preventing definitive recurrence assessment, the case is currently managed at a monitoring/investigation level and not classified as life-threatening. This suggests a potential degradation in performance of the device's arrhythmia detection capabilities, which requires investigation to understand the root cause and prevent future occurrences. The EU MDR mandates that electronic programmable systems are designed to ensure repeatability, reliability, and performance (mdr-annexI-sec17.1), and that appropriate measures should be adopted to eliminate or reduce risks in case of a single fault condition (mdr-annexI-sec17.2). Furthermore, the device is automated with computer software, triggering design control requirements under 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development). The missed detection, as evidenced by the confidence score logs (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A), warrants a CAPA investigation to determine if design or software lifecycle processes need adjustment.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "81db99d2c8f81767f958c31817ab98d549b9d950b6d3d4f0ce83d1f14d3c15ae", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_p